  "gameData": {
    "backstory": "Once a roadie for a Subchain City punk band, 'The Glitch Gobblers', Mute scavenges the ruins for forgotten power chords and spare drumsticks. The band's last gig ended in a DRIP riot, leaving Mute deafened and disillusioned, but armed with a trusty crow-killer and a thirst for payback.",
    "class": "Scavenger",
    "name": "Mute",
    "personality": "Grumpy: Mute is constantly scowling and muttering, a side effect of DRIP-induced tinnitus. Resourceful: Years on the road taught Mute how to fix anything with duct tape and scavenged wires. Loyal: Despite his gruff exterior, Mute fiercely protects his flock, recalling the brotherhood of his old band.",
    "specialAbility": {
      "description": "Mute can use his 'Crow-Killer' to disarm traps or stun enemies, creating a tactical advantage for his team. The blunt weapon is also good for prying open jammed containers or breaking down barricades, helping the flock get to the DRIP faster.",
